H900.definition:
feminine plural active participle of H898 (בָּגַד);
treacheries
KJV: treacherous.

H902.definition:
probably of foreign origin;
Bigvai, an Israelite
KJV: Bigvai.

H903.definition:
of Persian derivation;
Bigtha, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV: Bigtha.

H904.definition:
or בִּגְתָנָא; of similar derivation to H903 (בִּגְתָא);
Bigthan or Bigthana, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV: Bigthan, Bigthana.

H905.definition:
from H909 (בָּדַד);
properly, separation; by implication, a part of the body, branch of atree, bar forcarrying; figuratively, chief of a city; especially (with prepositional prefix) as an adverb, apart, only, besides
KJV: alone, apart, bar, besides, branch, by self, of each alike, except, only, part, staff, strength.

H906.definition:
perhaps from H909 (בָּדַד) (in the sense of divided fibres);
flaxen thread or yarn; hence, a linen garment
KJV: linen.

H907.definition:
from H908 (בָּדָא);
a brag or lie; also a liar
KJV: liar, lie.

H908.definition:
a primitive root;
(figuratively) to invent
KJV: devise, feign.

H909.definition:
a primitive root;
to divide, i.e. (reflex.) be solitary
KJV: alone.

H910.definition:
from H909 (בָּדַד);
separate; adverb, separately
KJV: alone, desolate, only, solitary.

H911.definition:
from H909 (בָּדַד); separation;
Bedad, an Edomite
KJV: Bedad.

H912.definition:
probably a shortened form H5662 (עֹבַדְיָה); servant of Jehovah;
Bedejah, an Israelite
KJV: Bedeiah.

H913.definition:
from H914 (בָּדַל);
alloy (because removed by smelting); by analogy, tin
KJV: [phrase] plummet, tin.

H914.definition:
a primitive root;
to divide (in variation senses literally or figuratively, separate, distinguish, differ, select, etc.)
KJV: (make, put) difference, divide (asunder), (make) separate (self, -ation), sever (out), [idiom] utterly.

H915.definition:
from H914 (בָּדַל);
a part
KJV: piece.

H916.definition:
probably from H914 (בָּדַל);
something in pieces, i.e. bdellium, a (fragrant) gum (perhaps amber); others a pearl
KJV: bdellium.

H917.definition:
probably shortened for H5658 (עַבְדוֹן); servile;
Bedan, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Bedan.

H918.definition:
a primitive root; to gap open; used only as a denominative from H919 (בֶּדֶק);
to mend a breach
KJV: repair.

H919.definition:
from H918 (בָּדַק);
a gap or leak (in a building or a ship)
KJV: breach, [phrase] calker.

H920.definition:
probably from H1856 (דָּקַר) with a prepositional prefix; by stabbing, i.e. assassin;
Bidkar, an Israelite
KJV: Bidkar.

H921.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding (by transposition) to H6504 (פָּרַד);
to scatter
KJV: scatter.

H922.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to be empty);
a vacuity, i.e. (superficially) an undistinguishable ruin
KJV: emptiness, void.

H923.definition:
from an unused root (probably meaning to glisten);
white marble or perhaps alabaster
KJV: red (marble).

H924.definition:
(Aramaic) from H927 (בְּהַל);
a hurry; only adverb, hastily
KJV: in haste.

H925.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to be bright);
shining
KJV: bright.

H926.definition:
a primitive root;
to tremble inwardly (or palpitate), i.e. (figuratively) be (causative, make) (suddenly) alarmed or agitated; by implication to hasten anxiously
KJV: be (make) affrighted (afraid, amazed, dismayed, rash), (be, get, make) haste(-n, -y, -ily), (give) speedy(-ily), thrust out, trouble, vex.

H927.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H926 (בָּהַל);
to terrify, hasten
KJV: in haste, trouble.

H928.definition:
from H926 (בָּהַל);
panic, destruction
KJV: terror, trouble.

H929.definition:
from an unused root (probably meaning to be mute);
properly, a dumb beast; especially any large quadruped or animal (often collective)
KJV: beast, cattle.

H930.definition:
in form a plural or H929 (בְּהֵמָה), but really a singular of Egyptian derivation;
a water-ox, i.e. the hippopotamus or Nile-horse
KJV: Behemoth.

H931.definition:
from an unused root apparently meaning to be thick;
the thumb of the hand or great toe of the foot
KJV: thumb, great toe.

H932.definition:
an orthographical variation of H931 (בֹּהֶן);
thumb, Bohan, an Israelite
KJV: Bohan.

H933.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be pale;
white scurf
KJV: freckled spot.

H934.definition:
feminine active participle of the same as H925 (בָּהִיר);
a whitish spot on the skin
KJV: bright spot.

H935.definition:
a primitive root;
to go or come (in a wide variety of applications)
KJV: abide, apply, attain, [idiom] be, befall, [phrase] besiege, bring (forth, in, into, to pass), call, carry, [idiom] certainly, (cause, let, thing for) to come (against, in, out, upon, to pass), depart, [idiom] doubtless again, [phrase] eat, [phrase] employ, (cause to) enter (in, into, -tering, -trance, -try), be fallen, fetch, [phrase] follow, get, give, go (down, in, to war), grant, [phrase] have, [idiom] indeed, (in-) vade, lead, lift (up), mention, pull in, put, resort, run (down), send, set, [idiom] (well) stricken (in age), [idiom] surely, take (in), way.

H936.definition:
a primitive root;
to disrespect
KJV: contemn, despise, [idiom] utterly.

H937.definition:
from H936 (בּוּז);
disrespect
KJV: contempt(-uously), despised, shamed.

H938.definition:
the same as H937 (בּוּז);
Buz, the name of a son of Nahor, and of an Israelite
KJV: Buz.

H939.definition:
feminine passive participle of H936 (בּוּז);
something scorned; an object of contempt
KJV: despised.

H940.definition:
patronymic from H938 (בּוּז);
a Buzite or descendant of Buz
KJV: Buzite.

H941.definition:
the same as H940 (בּוּזִי);
Buzi, an Israelite
KJV: Buzi.

H942.definition:
probably of Persian origin;
Bavvai, an Israelite
KJV: Bavai.

H943.definition:
a primitive root;
to involve (literally or figuratively)
KJV: be entangled, (perplexed).

H944.definition:
for H2981 (יְבוּל);
produce (of the earth, etc.)
KJV: food, stock.

H945.definition:
the same as H944 (בּוּל) (in the sense of rain);
Bul, the eighth Hebrew month
KJV: Bul.

H946.definition:
from H995 (בִּין); discretion;
Bunah, an Israelite
KJV: Bunah.

H947.definition:
a primitive root;
to trample (literally or figuratively)
KJV: loath, tread (down, under (foot)), be polluted.

H948.definition:
from an unused root (of the same form) meaning to bleach, i.e. (intransitive) be white;
probably cotton (of some sort)
KJV: fine (white) linen.

H949.definition:
from the same as H948 (בּוּץ); shining;
Botsets, a rock near Michmash
KJV: Bozez.

H950.definition:
feminine passive participle of an unused root (meaning to be hollow);
emptiness (as adjective)
KJV: empty.

H951.definition:
properly, active participle from H1239 (בָּקַר) as denominative from H1241 (בָּקָר);
a cattle-tender
KJV: herdman.

H952.definition:
a primitive root;
to bore, i.e. (figuratively) examine
KJV: declare.

H953.definition:
from H952 (בּוּר) (in the sense of H877 (בֹּאר));
a pit hole (especially one used as a cistern or a prison)
KJV: cistern, dungeon, fountain, pit, well.

H954.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to pale, i.e. by implication to be ashamed; also (by implication) to be disappointed or delayed
KJV: (be, make, bring to, cause, put to, with, a-) shamed(-d), be (put to) confounded(-fusion), become dry, delay, be long.

H955.definition:
feminine participle passive of H954 (בּוּשׁ);
shame
KJV: shame.

H956.definition:
(Aramaic) apparent denominative from H1005 (בַּיִת);
to lodge over night
KJV: pass the night.

H957.definition:
from H962 (בָּזַז);
plunder
KJV: booty, prey, spoil(-ed).

H958.definition:
a primitive root;
probably to cleave
KJV: spoil.

H959.definition:
a primitive root;
to disesteem
KJV: despise, disdain, contemn(-ptible), [phrase] think to scorn, vile person.

H961.definition:
feminine of H957 (בַּז);
booty
KJV: prey, spoil.

H962.definition:
a primitive root;
to plunder
KJV: catch, gather, (take) for a prey, rob(-ber), spoil, take (away, spoil), [idiom] utterly.

H964.definition:
from H959 (בָּזָה) and H3050 (יָהּ); contempts of Jah;
Bizjothjah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Bizjothjah.

H965.definition:
from an unused root meaning to lighten;
a flash of lightning
KJV: flash of lightning.

H966.definition:
from H965 (בָּזָק); lightning;
Bezek, a place in Palestine
KJV: Bezek.

H967.definition:
a primitive root;
to disperse
KJV: scatter.

H968.definition:
of Persian origin;
Biztha, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV: Biztha.

H969.definition:
from H974 (בָּחַן);
an assayer or metals
KJV: tower.

H970.definition:
or בָּחֻר; participle passive of H977 (בָּחַר);
properly, selected, i.e. a youth (often collective)
KJV: (choice) young (man), chosen, [idiom] hole.

H971.definition:
another form of H975 (בַּחַן);
a watch-tower of besiegers
KJV: tower.

H972.definition:
from H977 (בָּחַר);
select
KJV: choose, chosen one, elect.

H973.definition:
a primitive root;
to loath
KJV: abhor, get hastily (from the margin for H926 (בָּהַל)).

H974.definition:
a primitive root;
to test (especially metals); generally and figuratively, to investigate
KJV: examine, prove, tempt, try (trial).

H975.definition:
from H974 (בָּחַן) (in the sense of keeping a look-out);
a watch-tower
KJV: tower.

H977.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to try, i.e. (by implication) select
KJV: acceptable, appoint, choose (choice), excellent, join, be rather, require.

H978.definition:
patrial from H980 (בַּחֻרִים) (by transposition);
a Bacharumite or inhabitant of Bachurim
KJV: Baharumite.

H979.definition:
or בְּחוּרוֹת; feminine plural of H970 (בָּחוּר); also (masculine plural) בְּחֻרִים;
youth (collectively and abstractly)
KJV: young men, youth.

H980.definition:
or בַּחוּרִים; masculine plural of H970 (בָּחוּר); young men;
Bachurim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Bahurim.

H981.definition:
or בָּטָה; a primitive root;
to babble; hence, to vociferate angrily
KJV: pronounce, speak (unadvisedly).

H982.definition:
a primitive root; properly, to hide for refuge (but not so precipitately as H2620 (חָסָה));
figuratively, to trust, be confident or sure
KJV: be bold (confident, secure, sure), careless (one, woman), put confidence, (make to) hope, (put, make to) trust.

H983.definition:
from H982 (בָּטַח);
properly, a place of refuge; abstract, safety, both the fact (security) and the feeling (trust); often (adverb with or without preposition) safely
KJV: assurance, boldly, (without) care(-less), confidence, hope, safe(-ly, -ty), secure, surely.

H984.definition:
the same as H983 (בֶּטַח);
Betach, a place in Syria
KJV: Betah.

H985.definition:
feminine of H984 (בֶּטַח);
trust
KJV: confidence.

H986.definition:
from H982 (בָּטַח);
trust
KJV: confidence, hope.

H987.definition:
feminine plural from H982 (בָּטַח);
security
KJV: secure.

H988.definition:
a primitive root;
to desist from labor
KJV: cease.

H989.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H988 (בָּטֵל);
to stop
KJV: (cause, make to), cease, hinder.

H990.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to be hollow;
the belly, especially the womb; also the bosom or body of anything
KJV: belly, body, [phrase] as they be born, [phrase] within, womb.

H991.definition:
the same as H990 (בֶּטֶן);
Beten. a place in Palestine
KJV: Beten.

H992.definition:
from H990 (בֶּטֶן);
(only in plural) a pistachio-nut (from its form)
KJV: nut.

H993.definition:
probably plural from H992 (בֹּטֶן); hollows;
Betonim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Betonim.

H994.definition:
perhaps from H1158 (בָּעָה) (in the sense of asking); properly, a request; used only adverbially (always with 'my Lord');
oh that!; with leave, or if it please
KJV: alas, O, oh.

H995.definition:
a primitive root;
to separate mentally (or distinguish), i.e.(generally) understand
KJV: attend, consider, be cunning, diligently, direct, discern, eloquent, feel, inform, instruct, have intelligence, know, look well to, mark, perceive, be prudent, regard, (can) skill(-full), teach, think, (cause, make to, get, give, have) understand(-ing), view, (deal) wise(-ly, man).

H997.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H996 (בֵּין)
{between (repeated before each noun, often with other particles); also as a conjunction, either...or}
KJV: among, between.

H998.definition:
from H995 (בִּין);
understanding
KJV: knowledge, meaning, [idiom] perfectly, understanding, wisdom.
